{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in))) {\n            String[] parts = br.readLine().trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n            int a = Integer.parseInt(parts[0]);\n            int b = Integer.parseInt(parts[1]);\n            int l = Integer.parseInt(parts[2]);\n            int r = Integer.parseInt(parts[3]);\n            System.out.println(process(a, b, l, r));\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            System.err.println(\"Error: \" + e.getMessage());\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static int process(int a, int b, int l, int r) {\n        int total = a + b;\n        if (r - l + 1 > 2 * total) {\n            return a <= b ? a + 1 : 2 * a - b;\n        }\n\n        int[] arr = new int[3 * total + 1];\n        int prev = 0;\n\n        for (int i = 1; i <= a; i++) {\n            arr[i] = i;\n            prev = i;\n        }\n\n        for (int i = a + 1; i <= total; i++) {\n            arr[i] = prev;\n        }\n\n        for (int i = total + 1; i <= total + a; i++) {\n            int candidate = 1;\n            while (check(arr, candidate, total - a + 1, i - 1)) {\n                candidate++;\n            }\n            arr[i] = candidate;\n            prev = candidate;\n        }\n\n        for (int i = total + a + 1; i <= 2 * total; i++) {\n            arr[i] = prev;\n        }\n\n        for (int i = 2 * total + 1; i <= 3 * total; i++) {\n            arr[i] = arr[i - total];\n        }\n\n        boolean[] found = new boolean[25];\n        int start = l % total;\n        if (start == 0) start += total;\n        int finish = r - l + start;\n        if (finish < start) finish += total;\n\n        for (int idx = start; idx <= finish; idx++) {\n            if (idx < arr.length) found[arr[idx]] = true;\n        }\n\n        int unique = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= 24; i++) {\n            if (found[i]) unique++;\n        }\n        return unique;\n    }\n\n    private static boolean check(int[] data, int value, int left, int right) {\n        for (int i = left; i <= right; i++) {\n            if (i < data.length && data[i] == value) return true;\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <sstream>\n#include <cstring>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nbool check(const vector<int>& data, int value, int left, int right) {\n    for (int i = left; i <= right; i++) {\n        if (i < (int)data.size() && data[i] == value) return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n}\n\nint process(int a, int b, int l, int r) {\n    int total = a + b;\n    if (r - l + 1 > 2 * total) {\n        return a <= b ? a + 1 : 2 * a - b;\n    }\n\n    vector<int> arr(3 * total + 1, 0);\n    int prev = 0;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i <= a; i++) {\n        arr[i] = i;\n        prev = i;\n    }\n\n    for (int i = a + 1; i <= total; i++) {\n        arr[i] = prev;\n    }\n\n    for (int i = total + 1; i <= total + a; i++) {\n        int candidate = 1;\n        while (check(arr, candidate, total - a + 1, i - 1)) {\n            candidate++;\n        }\n        arr[i] = candidate;\n        prev = candidate;\n    }\n\n    for (int i = total + a + 1; i <= 2 * total; i++) {\n        arr[i] = prev;\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 2 * total + 1; i <= 3 * total; i++) {\n        arr[i] = arr[i - total];\n    }\n\n    vector<bool> found(25, false);\n    int start = l % total;\n    if (start == 0) start += total;\n    int finish = r - l + start;\n    if (finish < start) finish += total;\n\n    for (int idx = start; idx <= finish; idx++) {\n        if (idx < (int)arr.size()) found[arr[idx]] = true;\n    }\n\n    int unique = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= 24; i++) {\n        if (found[i]) unique++;\n    }\n    return unique;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    string line;\n    if (!getline(cin, line)) {\n        cerr << \"Error: Failed to read input\" << endl;\n        return 1;\n    }\n    \n    istringstream iss(line);\n    vector<string> parts;\n    string part;\n    while (iss >> part) {\n        parts.push_back(part);\n    }\n    \n    if (parts.size() < 4) {\n        cerr << \"Error: Not enough input values\" << endl;\n        return 1;\n    }\n    \n    try {\n        int a = stoi(parts[0]);\n        int b = stoi(parts[1]);\n        int l_val = stoi(parts[2]);\n        int r_val = stoi(parts[3]);\n        cout << process(a, b, l_val, r_val) << endl;\n    } catch (const exception& e) {\n        cerr << \"Error: \" << e.what() << endl;\n        return 1;\n    }\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.989239333663136e-05, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.000575376907363534, -1.311301275563892e-06, -3.933898824470816e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.4798915982246399, -5.960462772